# {{ project_name }} — Development Instructions

## Architecture and Boundaries

- Follow Clean Architecture dependency direction: `core ← infrastructure/ai ← application ← presentation`
- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/core/` must remain framework-independent — no imports from infrastructure/presentation
- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/application/` can import from `core` and configuration, but not concrete adapters
- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/infrastructure/` implements protocols declared in `core/interfaces/`
- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/composition/` wires everything together via the `Container` DI pattern
- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/presentation/api/` contains FastAPI routers
{% if api_style in ('graphql', 'both') %}- `backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/presentation/graphql/` contains Strawberry GraphQL schema and resolvers
{% endif %}

## Backend Stack

- Python {{ python_version }}+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2.0+ async, Alembic
{% if api_style in ('graphql', 'both') %}- Strawberry GraphQL (subscriptions)
{% endif %}- Settings: `{{ project_slug }}.config.settings.get_settings()` — env-specific subclasses of `BaseAppConfig`
- Enums: `ParseableEnum(StrEnum)` + `@unique` + explicit values in `{{ project_slug }}.core.enums/`
- DI Container: `{{ project_slug }}.composition.Container` with `@cached_property`
- Testing: pytest, hypothesis, factory-boy, pytest-asyncio, pytest-benchmark
- Naming registry: `registry/naming_registry.json` → generated constants
- Linting: ruff (`backend/ruff.toml`), ty for type checking

## Frontend Stack

- React 19, TypeScript, Vite 6 + SWC, Bun
- UI: shadcn/ui (Radix + Tailwind CSS v4) — use CLI (`bunx shadcn@latest add`), never copy-paste
- State: Zustand, TanStack React Query
- Linting: Biome (not Prettier/ESLint)
- Testing: Vitest + React Testing Library + fast-check, Playwright for E2E

## Project Layout

- `tasks/` — Split Taskfile includes (backend.yml, frontend.yml)
- `registry/` — Naming registry JSON + code generator

## Tooling and Commands

- Use `uv` for Python dependency and command execution
- Use `bun` for frontend package management and scripts
- Root `Taskfile.yml` orchestrates via includes from `tasks/`
- Run `task check` (lint + tests + typecheck) before finalizing changes

## Quality Rules

- Keep changes minimal and scoped
- Update docs in the same change when behavior or setup changes
- Use typed Python signatures; avoid `Any` unless truly unavoidable
- Use `Final[type]` for module-level constants
- Use `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` for all dataclasses (except `Container`)
- Use `cn()` for Tailwind class merging; semantic color tokens only

## Security Rules

- Never commit secrets
- Keep `.env.example` updated when new environment variables are introduced

